      "writtenOn": "2021-01-25T11:55:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e This really should be discussed upstream first. I also wonder why this isn\u0027t directly a hook on panic(), which would cover two of the three hooks.\n\nbad_mode()/arm64_serror_panic() will call panic().\nBut panic_notifier cannot get other information like \u0027regs\u0027 and \u0027esr\u0027.\nBecause we can see PC/LR from \u0027regs\u0027 and a exception class and ISS data from \u0027esr\u0027, these information is useful for our Auto Comment and Market issue monitoring features mentioned in Bug: 177483057.\n\n\u003e Finally, I\u0027m worried about the safety of the NMI context, as you can\u0027t use much of the kernel constructs there.\n\nOur hooks are performing a simple procedure that it stores information into pre-allocated buffer without interacting with kernel constructs.\n\nEx)\na_hook(regs, esr)\n{\n   buf \u003d Auto Comment buffer\n   str \u003d make human readable string with \u0027regs\u0027 and \u0027esr\u0027\n   store \u0027str\u0027 into \u0027buf\u0027\n\n   arr \u003d Issue monitoring buffer\n   store regs-\u003epc into arr[PC]\n   store regs-\u003elr into arr[LR]\n   store regs-\u003eesr into arr[ESR]\n}",
      "parentUuid": "265a4c09_c9e68019",
      "revId": "145036233d366d60fa4ba639f5e14c58a900f63c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
